---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Command from "../components/Command.astro";
import { GUIDE, RELEASES, INSTALL_CMD, BREW_CMD } from "../site";
---

<Base
  title="Install"
  description="Install rlord with one command, or with Homebrew, a .deb or .rpm package, or Cargo. Then install the hooks and open the list."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Install</p>
      <h1>Install rlord</h1>
      <p class="lede">One command on macOS or Linux. Packages and a source build are below.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <Command cmd={INSTALL_CMD} label="Copy the install command" />
      <p>
        This installs the latest release for your machine to <code>~/.local/bin/rlord</code> and verifies its
        checksum. If tmux is missing, it offers to install it.
      </p>

      <h2 id="other">Other ways to install</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="stack">
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Homebrew (macOS, Linux)</th>
              <td><code>{BREW_CMD}</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Debian, Ubuntu</th>
              <td>
                <code>sudo apt install ./rlord_&lt;version&gt;_&lt;arch&gt;.deb</code> from{" "}
                <a href={RELEASES}>releases</a>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Fedora, RHEL, Amazon Linux</th>
              <td>
                <code>sudo dnf install ./rlord-&lt;version&gt;.&lt;arch&gt;.rpm</code> from{" "}
                <a href={RELEASES}>releases</a>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Cargo</th>
              <td><code>cargo install robot-overlord</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">From source</th>
              <td>
                <code>cargo build --release</code>, then put <code>target/release/rlord</code> on your PATH
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Prebuilt for Apple Silicon Macs and for Linux on x86_64 and ARM. The Linux build is static and runs on any distro.</p>

      <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>tmux 3.2 or newer.</li>
        <li>
          At least one agent: <a href="https://claude.com/claude-code">Claude Code</a>,{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex">Codex CLI</a> or <a href="https://opencode.ai">OpenCode</a> v2.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <code>rlord agents</code> shows which agents you have and the install command for one you don't. rlord never
        installs agents itself.
      </p>

      <h2 id="first-steps">First steps</h2>
      <pre class="block"><code><span class="c"># Once. Lets rlord see what your agents are doing.</span>
<span class="c"># Claude Code, and Codex if it is installed. OpenCode needs none.</span>
rlord install-hooks

<span class="c"># Open the list.</span>
rlord</code></pre>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Key</th>
              <th scope="col">What it does</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><kbd>Option-O</kbd> (Alt-O)</th>
              <td>Open the overlord and say what you want</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><kbd>n</kbd></th>
              <td>Start a new session. Describe it and the overlord sets it up.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><kbd>enter</kbd></th>
              <td>Attach to the selected session</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><kbd>Option-D</kbd> (Alt-D)</th>
              <td>Go back to the list from any session</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><kbd>?</kbd></th>
              <td>Show every key. <kbd>:</kbd> opens commands.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        On a Mac, set your terminal to send Option as Alt or Meta. In iTerm2 that is <em>Esc+</em>, in Ghostty{" "}
        <code>macos-option-as-alt</code>, and in Terminal <em>Use Option as Meta key</em>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you already have Claude Code sessions, ask the overlord to "import my sessions from the last week".
      </p>

      <h2 id="configuration">Configuration</h2>
      <p>
        Everything is optional. <code>rlord config init</code> writes a commented{" "}
        <code>~/.config/robot-overlord/config.toml</code>. It covers the layout, theme, keys, the Usage column, the
        default agent for new sessions, the overlord's agent, model and effort, archive summaries and the update
        channel. Standing instructions for the overlord go in <code>~/.config/robot-overlord/overlord.md</code>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="updating">Updating</h2>
      <pre class="block"><code>rlord update</code></pre>
      <p>Homebrew and distro packages update the usual way.</p>

      <p style="margin-top:2.5rem">The <a href={GUIDE}>user guide</a> covers each part in detail.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
